            "review_title": "Review at De L'amour Bistro & Cafe",
            "review_text": "AndrewTMAO\nSingapore, Singapore1170 contributions\n0\nShould be rated higher on TripAdvisor\nAug 2016 • Solo\nThe restaurant is tucked in behind the Opera House and close to Hanoi Hilton, it is a nice little find.\n\nI ordered foie gras which is often overcooked in Asia. Unfortunately in Vietnam, due to hygiene issues the liver is frozen rather than fresh. It was cooked perfectly and had a delightful raspberry sauce. At 299,000 quite reasonably priced.\n\nI followed with Chicken Cordon Bleu. WOW. Fantastic dish with a divine mushroom sauce. Again only 299,000.\n\nNot cheap by Vietnamese standards but quality was high and service was great.\nRead more\nWritten August 17, 2016",
